<title>GREECE: XIOSBANK CUTS CONSUMER LOAN RATE BY 100BPS TO 22PCT.</title>
<headline>XIOSBANK CUTS CONSUMER LOAN RATE BY 100BPS TO 22PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Xiosbank, which has filed</p>
<p>for listing on the Athens bourse will cut the base rate on its</p>
<p>consumer Polydaneion loan by 100 basis points to 22 percent, it</p>
<p>said in a statement.</p>
<p>The base rate for business credit will remain unchanged at</p>
<p>18.75 percent and its Xios Alma deposit account will offer an</p>
<p>annual yield of 11.57 percent with monthly interest payments.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
